  "id": "Compound::DB00471 - Disease::DOID:3083",
  "verbalization": "Montelukast, through its role in causing Skin Infection and Tonsillitis, indirectly contributes to the development of Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). The evidence suggests that Montelukast may influence the body's inflammatory response, potentially leading to conditions like Skin Infection or Tonsillitis, which in turn could exacerbate respiratory issues. The shared pathway involves Tiotropium and Formoterol, both of which are used to treat COPD, indicating a possible mechanistic link between Montelukast and the respiratory system. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role of Montelukast in modulating inflammatory processes that may contribute to COPD, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Montelukast may influence respiratory health through indirect pathways involving inflammatory conditions, but further research is needed to confirm this relationship.",
